SIMPLIFY PROJECTS COMPLETELY — Projects should only organize chats

We are changing the Product direction for Projects.

The current Project workspace became unnecessarily complex.

Remove the recent Project workspace complexity and make Projects extremely simple.

A Project should behave like a folder for BlueMind conversations.

Nothing more for now.

⸻

CORE CONCEPT

Project = named folder containing chats

Example:

Project:
BlueMind

Inside:

* Chat 1
* Chat 2
* Chat 3

The user can create/open chats inside that Project.

Those chats use the existing BlueMind Chat experience.

⸻

REMOVE FROM PROJECTS

Remove the Project frontend sections/features for:

* Files
* Tasks
* Notes
* Project content dashboard
* complex Overview content
* any workspace cards added specifically for those features
* any placeholder pages for Files / Tasks / Notes

Do not leave dead navigation into those sections.

We may rebuild advanced Projects later.

⸻

KEEP PROJECTS SIMPLE

The Projects area should allow only:

1. Create Project

User enters a Project name.

Example:

BlueMind

School

Work

Create it using existing backend persistence if available.

Do not fake persistence.

⸻

2. Project list

Show the user’s Projects in a clean native iOS list/cards.

Each Project may show:

* Project name
* number of chats if available
* last activity if already supported

Keep it minimal.

⸻

3. Open Project

Opening a Project should show only its chats.

Header:

←   Project Name

and a compact:

+ New Chat

Then show the conversations belonging to that Project.

No Files / Tasks / Notes tabs.

⸻

PROJECT CHAT LIST

Each Project chat row should show:

* chat title
* latest-message preview if available
* updated date/time if available

Tapping it opens the existing BlueMind Chat interface.

Do NOT build a second chat UI.

⸻

NEW CHAT INSIDE PROJECT

If the user taps:

+ New Chat

from Project A,

the new conversation must be associated with Project A.

Reuse the current chat infrastructure.

Preserve a stable:

projectId

or equivalent existing association.

If the backend already supports this, use it.

If it does not, report that clearly instead of pretending it is persisted.

⸻

MOVE EXISTING CHAT TO PROJECT

This is important.

In the menu/actions for a normal existing conversation outside Projects, add:

Move to Project

When tapped:

open a compact native iOS sheet/menu listing the user’s Projects.

Example:

Move to Project

* BlueMind
* School
* Work

User selects one Project.

The chat becomes associated with that Project.

After success:

show the global toast:

Chat moved to BlueMind

⸻

IMPORTANT MOVE BEHAVIOR

Moving a chat must NOT:

* duplicate the chat
* erase its messages
* create a second conversation
* reset its history

It should simply change the Project association of the existing conversation.

⸻

OPTIONAL: REMOVE FROM PROJECT

If a chat is already inside a Project, its conversation menu may include:

Remove from Project

This should return it to the normal ungrouped chat list without deleting the conversation.

Only implement this if the existing data architecture safely supports a nullable project association.

⸻

PROJECT MANAGEMENT

Keep Project management minimal.

At most:

* Create Project
* Rename Project
* Delete Project

Before Project deletion, inspect the backend behavior carefully.

Do NOT accidentally delete all conversations unless that is explicitly intended and confirmed.

Prefer safe behavior:

deleting the Project should either:

* move its chats back to ungrouped chats

or

* follow the existing backend contract.

Do not invent destructive behavior silently.

